  "body_markdown": "Skip to content\n\nDental Implants\n\nDental Implant Surgery\n\nAll-on-4 Dental Implants\n\nFixed Teeth vs. Removable\n\nCost & Compare\n\nDental Implant FAQ\n\nAesthetics\n\nCosmetic Dentistry\n\nPorcelain Veneers\n\nDental Crowns & Bridges\n\nSmile Makeover\n\nTeeth Whitening\n\nTreatments\n\nSedation Dentistry\n\nOral Surgery\n\nEmergency Dentistry\n\nConditions We Treat\n\nWhat To Expect\n\nPatient Center\n\nInsurance & Financing\n\nSmile Gallery\n\nWho We Are\n\nWhy Choose Us\n\nMeet Dr. Esam Nahlah\n\nMeet The Team\n\nVideo Library\n\nPatient Stories\n\nFor Doctors\n\nReferral Form\n\nContact Us\n\nBlog\n\nCurrent Patients\n\nTysons Corner: (703) 448-3312\n\nAlexandria: (703) 940-5410\n\nNew Patients\n\nTysons Corner: (571) 619-9442\n\nAlexandria: (571) 410-3430\n\nBook now\n\n\n## Book Now\n\n\n\n## Book Now\n\n\n\n## How Exactly Do Implant Supported Dentures In McLean, VA Benefit My Smile?\n\n\nOctober 5, 2023\n\n\n#### Share This Post\n\n\nImplant supported dentures in McLean, VA are a tooth replacement option that uses dental implants to support a denture. If people don’t replace their missing teeth with implant supported dentures, they run the risk of losing jawbone density, losing dental functionality, and losing the confidence to show their smile.\n\nLuckily, implant supported dentures can benefit patients’ smiles in many ways. Continue reading to learn in more detail how implant supported dentures benefit patients’ smiles.\n\n\n## How Implant Supported Dentures In McLean, VA Benefit My Smiles\n\n\nHere are the specific ways that implant supported dentures can benefit patient’s smiles:\n\n\n### Dentures Are Made from Acrylic or Porcelain Material:\n\n\nThe dentures for implant-supported procedures can be made from either acrylic or porcelain material. Both materials offer unique advantages. Acrylic, being lightweight and less expensive, can be more comfortable and affordable for patients. On the other hand, porcelain dentures are renowned for their durability and natural appearance. They are resistant to wear and stains, making them a long-lasting tooth replacement option.\n\n\n### Two or More Dental Implants Support the Denture:\n\n\nTwo or more dental implants are used to support the denture in an implant-supported denture procedure. These dental implants are strategically placed into the patient’s jawbone, giving their denture a secure and stable foundation to be attached to.\n\nThe number of dental implants needed in an implant supported denture procedure varies from patient to patient. With the two or more dental implants, the denture stays in place in the patient’s mouth, preventing them from slipping or causing the patient discomfort. Securely placed implant supported dentures also help patients eat and speak properly, improving the functionality of their mouth.\n\n\n### Restores Dental Stability:\n\n\nImplant supported dentures effectively prevent the denture from slipping, loosening, or falling out of the patient’s mouth. Dental implants, which are made to function like natural tooth roots, serve as a sturdy foundation for dentures to be attached to.\n\nWhen dental implants fuse with the patient’s jawbone over time, they become a permanent part of their smile. This restored dental stability means that the dentures are securely held in place, preventing them from slipping, loosening, or falling out of the patient’s jawbone. With implant supported dentures, patients get a stable and secure new smile.\n\n\n### Improves Jawbone Health:\n\n\nImplant supported dentures play a pivotal role in maintaining and improving jawbone health. Besides giving patients a permanent new smile, when the dental implant posts are placed in the patient’s jawbone, it stimulates it so its volume and density are restored.\n\nWith a restored jawbone, implant supported denture patients won’ t have to worry about jawbone resorption or having a sunken-in looking face. By replacing their missing teeth with implant supported dentures, patients not only enhance the look of their smile, they also improve their overall oral health by preserving their jawbone.\n\n\n## See Us Now So Your Smile Can Benefit From Our Quality Implant Supported Dentures\n\n\nAre you tired of dealing with uncomfortable and unstable traditional dentures? Do you want to replace your missing teeth with a reliable and trusted tooth replacement option? When you upgrade your smile with our state-of-the-art implant supported dentures, you will be able to eat, speak, and smile comfortably, and confidently. If properly taken care of, implant supported dentures can enhance your smile for years to come.\n\nWhile implant supported dentures may not look completely natural in your mouth, they will give you brand-new teeth that you can feel confident in. Don’t hesitate to improve the look, function, and health of your smile with us. Get in contact with our doctors, Dr. Esam Nahlah and our exceptional team at our office to schedule an appointment today!\n\nPrevPreviousAfter My Dental Implants Are Placed, How Will I Know If I Have Peri-Implantitis?\n\nNextDo I Need A Full Mouth Dental Implant Consultation?Next\n\n\n#### More To Explore\n\n\n\n### Unlock the Benefits of Dental Implants: Your Best Teeth Replacement Option\n\n\nTooth loss can become an unfortunate reality for many as we age. Thankfully, advancements in dental technology, like dental implants,\n\nRead More »\n\nOctober 26, 2024\n\n\n### Your Comprehensive Guide on Dental Implants: The Best Replacement of Tooth Solution\n\n\nDental implants in McLean, VA are small, and titanium posts are surgically placed in your jawbone underneath your gum line.\n\nOctober 20, 2024\n\n\n## You Are Welcome Here.\n\n\nSchedule your consultation today.\n\nFacebook Instagram Youtube Google\n\n\n#### Contact Us\n\n\nAddresses:\n\nTysons Corner\n\n7901 Jones Branch Dr., Suite 220\n\nMcLean, VA 22102\n\nNew Patients: (571) 619-9442\n\nCurrent Patients: (703) 448-3312\n\nAlexandria\n\n2855 Duke St,\n\nAlexandria, VA 22314\n\nNew Patients: (571) 410-3430\n\nCurrent Patients: (703) 940-5410\n\n\n#### Hours\n\n\nMonday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nTuesday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nWednesday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nThursday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nFriday: 8:00am – 2:00pm\n\nSaturday: Closed\n\nSunday: Closed\n\n\n#### Services\n\n\nAll-On-4® Implants\n\nCrowns & Bridges\n\n\n#### About Us\n\n\nMeet the Doctor\n\nAbout Us\n\nBefore & After Photos\n\n2025 Dr. Nahlah. All rights reserved",
